1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,080
To each their own, but personally, I think Miyamura looks best with long hair.

2
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:17,320
They're making a sequel! Part two of that horror flick I love is in the works!

3
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:18,580
Whoa, really?

4
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:25,280
I felt drawn to him as a fellow bespectacled classmate, since our numbers are few.

5
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:28,320
And his long hair gave him an air of mystery.

6
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:30,820
It was sensational.

7
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:35,680
Watabe! Did you find that reference book I asked for, or...?

8
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:37,740
I say we go see it on opening day.

9
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:41,320
Uh, sure, it's a date. Yay.

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,060
That said, this fun-loving Miyamura's nice, too.

11
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:46,840
I approve.

12
00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:50,160
Yo! Watch Step-Up Pick a Miyamura!

13
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:51,980
To memorialize him?

14
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:54,680
Now I have even more questions.

15
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:02,320
Share this video.

16
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:03,680
See ya.

17
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:22,260
Our friend, the

18
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:52,240
Thank you.

19
00:01:52,260 --> 00:02:22,240
Thank you.

20
00:02:22,260 --> 00:02:24,260
Thank you.

21
00:02:52,260 --> 00:02:54,180
Horty's the huge horror buff, not me.

22
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:57,340
Bet the pair of you would be friends at first fright, huh?

23
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:01,560
Uh, well, it's hard to say.

24
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:06,200
But, uh, I still enjoy it even though I'm not a fanatic.

25
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:07,320
Oh, you do?

26
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:08,360
That's so great!

27
00:03:08,460 --> 00:03:09,720
It means we share a hobby now.

28
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:10,960
Yeah.

29
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:16,960
It's like I can feel the hearts floating off his sleeves and into my personal space.

30
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:19,400
Oh, common interests are so fun.

31
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:21,780
Here, check these other books out, Miyamura.

32
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:22,400
Okay.

33
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:26,380
Hey, everybody.

34
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:29,080
You're just in time for a special treat.

35
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:31,560
How does a steaming cup of chow and mushy sound?

36
00:03:31,820 --> 00:03:34,020
Goodbye, yours truly, so you know it still is.

37
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,100
Ah, thanks, Kiyosuke.

38
00:03:36,100 --> 00:03:39,120
But what makes this one special is the ginkgo nuts.

39
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:41,620
And it was my idea to add them in the first place.

40
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:43,380
Oh, that was a good call.

41
00:03:43,880 --> 00:03:45,260
Like father, like son.

42
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:48,480
Huh?

43
00:03:49,060 --> 00:03:50,480
Hey, I was wondering when you...

44
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:50,720
Stop!

45
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:58,820
Did I stink?

46
00:03:59,540 --> 00:04:00,640
Of Watabe funk.

47
00:04:02,140 --> 00:04:04,640
Normally, there's a trace of Toru or Shindo.

48
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:06,260
This is cursing my wimp, I've been.

49
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:06,980
I can't breathe.

50
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:08,760
While I'm choking on that stench.

51
00:04:09,420 --> 00:04:12,060
How you know what Watabe smells like is the real question.

52
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:14,920
I took samples in case the scenario played out.

53
00:04:15,620 --> 00:04:16,560
What scenario?

54
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:20,200
You can smell people's scent on me even if we just talk?

55
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:22,240
Female scents do not compute.

56
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:23,940
The only ones that do are male.

57
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:25,180
And now you're a robot?

58
00:04:26,260 --> 00:04:27,780
I don't smell a thing.

59
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:30,580
You don't have to detect any strange aromas.

60
00:04:30,840 --> 00:04:31,920
What counts as I can?

61
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:34,100
But I kind of want to.

62
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:36,820
So I'll be able to tell if you've been with someone else.

63
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:38,900
Be it hanging out or...

64
00:04:38,900 --> 00:04:40,820
I see.

65
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:46,180
What you really want is a means to determine if I surround myself with guys all day the same way that you do.

66
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:48,200
That phrasing irked me a little bit.

67
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:49,800
But yeah, basically.

68
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:52,260
Well, I don't.

69
00:04:52,980 --> 00:04:54,920
Um, we both know that's a lie.

70
00:04:55,340 --> 00:04:56,380
I can think of two.

71
00:04:56,740 --> 00:04:59,120
You always hang around with Ishikawa and the Prez.

72
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:02,000
But I'd never know that just by getting a good whiff of you.

73
00:05:02,620 --> 00:05:04,020
How about we make a deal then?

74
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:06,400
If I cheat, I'll tell you to your face.

75
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:09,740
That'd be a big help.

76
00:05:09,940 --> 00:05:10,360
Thought so.

77
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:11,740
Dude is ready!

78
00:05:11,740 --> 00:05:16,400
She went ballistic.

79
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:18,120
I'm talking vain, popping mad.

80
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:21,900
Like, I've never been the best at studying, so I have no clue why.

81
00:05:22,460 --> 00:05:25,920
But I guess I could buckle down and really apply myself, huh?

82
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:27,000
Worth a try.

83
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,840
It could be a whole lot worse, Ishikawa.

84
00:05:30,220 --> 00:05:32,840
If I so much as play a CD, the cord gets yanked out.

85
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:33,700
No tunes.

86
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:36,180
Music helps stimulate the brain, though, doesn't it?

87
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:38,540
All of their expectations are sky high.

88
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:40,620
Can't they see we're doing our best down here?

89
00:05:40,620 --> 00:05:44,660
The heck?

90
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:46,900
I can't tell.

91
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:47,920
Yeah.

92
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:49,700
How much you want to bet it's hoodie-related?

93
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:51,460
Two, no, three million.

94
00:05:51,820 --> 00:05:53,060
They're just weirdos.

95
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:54,580
It's the core of who they are.

96
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:57,840
What's up?

97
00:05:58,300 --> 00:06:00,160
I hardly ever get invited to your place.

98
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:02,900
Though I always love it when I do.

99
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:05,400
Oh, but you can hang on to that controller.

100
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:06,740
I have more at home.

101
00:06:06,980 --> 00:06:08,920
That's not the reason I asked you to come over.

102
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:10,760
And even if you want it, you can't have it.

103
00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:13,420
Then what's the deal, dude?

104
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:17,640
I...

105
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:19,840
I want you to close your eyes.

106
00:06:20,140 --> 00:06:20,560
Huh?

107
00:06:21,540 --> 00:06:23,980
Are you going to do something to me?

108
00:06:24,620 --> 00:06:24,940
Yeah.

109
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:26,320
No way.

110
00:06:27,300 --> 00:06:28,320
It'll be over quick.

111
00:06:28,940 --> 00:06:29,440
What, Will?

112
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:31,380
You can end so many things in a moment.

113
00:06:31,860 --> 00:06:32,940
Including my life!

114
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:35,680
Then explain if I thought you'd get it.

115
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:37,080
Just close your eyes.

116
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:38,800
What for?

117
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:41,380
What are you going to do once you rob me of my life, Miyamura?

118
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:41,960
Fine!

119
00:06:42,260 --> 00:06:44,420
You can look, but shut up and sit still!

120
00:06:50,340 --> 00:06:50,820
There.

121
00:06:51,520 --> 00:06:53,560
If anyone made a move, it'd be you.

122
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:55,820
But I have your scent memorized now.

123
00:06:56,360 --> 00:06:56,860
Time out.

124
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:59,180
Who am I making moves on?

125
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:00,140
Shut up!

126
00:07:00,140 --> 00:07:27,200
I'm going to ask you anyway, because no one else will.

127
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:29,580
Are you listening?

128
00:07:29,580 --> 00:07:31,280
Oh, I'm sorry.

129
00:07:31,700 --> 00:07:35,440
Once I save these babies in my Miyamura folder, I'll be all ears.

130
00:07:35,940 --> 00:07:38,600
I hear your camera snapping pictures like there's no tomorrow.

131
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:40,720
Do you have a folder just for Miyamura?

132
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:41,560
A sketch?

133
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:45,740
But yeah, so my hesitant question.

134
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:48,460
Are you crushing on Miyamura?

135
00:07:49,100 --> 00:07:51,300
It goes far beyond that level of attachment.

136
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:53,780
I find him greatly fascinating.

137
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:55,480
I can't explain it.

138
00:07:55,480 --> 00:08:00,220
But there's Hori, his ever-charming girl.

139
00:08:00,540 --> 00:08:01,340
I don't follow.

140
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:03,280
You speak as if that's a bad thing?

141
00:08:03,740 --> 00:08:06,640
Miyamura dating the opposite sex is moe.

142
00:08:06,860 --> 00:08:10,540
If you're a fan, then you're aware he has guy friends from other schools, yeah?

143
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:11,520
You know, like Shindo?

144
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:15,280
There are boys outside of the school he has affection for.

145
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:18,640
Creepy.

146
00:08:19,140 --> 00:08:20,720
No, he's a pal, not a creep.

147
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:22,700
Don't think of pals as creeps.

148
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:27,720
Okay, so you just admire him from afar?

149
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:29,660
I'd love to touch him one day.

150
00:08:30,020 --> 00:08:30,620
Oh, wow.

151
00:08:30,780 --> 00:08:31,960
Okay, let me rephrase that.

152
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:34,800
Like, do you ever want to talk to the guy?

153
00:08:34,840 --> 00:08:37,360
I don't have that desire since I recorded him.

154
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:38,460
What's up, Watabe?

155
00:08:39,400 --> 00:08:41,840
I am extremely concerned.

156
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:43,000
Hey!

157
00:08:44,040 --> 00:08:45,780
Come play some ping-pong!

158
00:08:48,860 --> 00:08:52,340
Ishikawa, if an asteroid that was two kilometers in width

159
00:08:52,340 --> 00:08:53,900
crashed into me at this very moment,

160
00:08:54,160 --> 00:08:55,720
I'd die a happy soul.

161
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:57,040
No regrets.

162
00:08:57,640 --> 00:09:00,900
A space rock that size would kill Miyamura on Impact 2, you know.

163
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:04,360
Eureak!

164
00:09:04,820 --> 00:09:05,860
Watabe, bitch!

165
00:09:05,860 --> 00:09:07,480
It fellin' all over you!

166
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:11,180
Now, for some reason, it's much stronger today.

167
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:12,940
He thinks he's marking his territory.

168
00:09:12,940 --> 00:09:14,460
He's gonna rephrase!

169
00:09:16,140 --> 00:09:18,920
You're saying I smell worse than usual?

170
00:09:19,340 --> 00:09:21,360
I didn't even notice him get that close.

171
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:24,220
There are also hints of Shindo and Tanihara on you,

172
00:09:24,340 --> 00:09:26,460
but Watabe's stink overpowers them both.

173
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:28,500
And why wouldn't it?

174
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:31,340
His odor is as intense as his interest in you,

175
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:34,360
an obsession that puts the other boys in your life to shame.

176
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:37,120
How can you know all that from someone's B.O.?

177
00:09:37,120 --> 00:09:40,520
I'm telling you, despite what your nose detects,

178
00:09:40,520 --> 00:09:42,000
I didn't lay a finger on that kid.

179
00:09:42,180 --> 00:09:44,720
Doesn't matter how many fingers came into contact with him.

180
00:09:44,720 --> 00:10:01,820
You're scent is the only one I would know anywhere.

181
00:10:01,820 --> 00:10:05,900
You'd think that'd also be true for girls like Yoshikawa or Ayasaki.

182
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:11,680
I thought you'd finally do it.

183
00:10:11,940 --> 00:10:12,240
Huh?

184
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:14,300
The way you whipped around.

185
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:17,800
I thought you were gonna manhandle me into next week!

186
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:19,940
Quit getting my hopes up, you T's!

187
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,840
I can't believe they were high enough to make you cry when they fell!

188
00:10:23,020 --> 00:10:23,500
I'm sorry!

189
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:24,560
You dummy!

190
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:26,600
Don't you dare touch me now!

191
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:29,700
Enough with the deodorizer spray!

192
00:10:29,700 --> 00:10:39,100
Traffic accident?

193
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:40,080
No.

194
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:41,560
It was man-made.

195
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:42,480
Howdy, huh?

196
00:10:42,900 --> 00:10:43,560
Oh, boy.

197
00:10:43,820 --> 00:10:44,980
So you two fought again?

198
00:10:45,380 --> 00:10:45,900
Mm-hmm.

199
00:10:46,040 --> 00:10:48,120
I don't know who won, but she got you good.

200
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:50,380
I don't care what she says or does.

201
00:10:50,420 --> 00:10:52,320
I'm not apologizing this time around.

202
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:54,800
Morning.

203
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:57,520
Hori, what happened to your face?

204
00:10:57,840 --> 00:10:59,020
Ugh, that must hurt.

205
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:00,980
Dude, did you hit her back?

206
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:02,260
No, no!

207
00:11:05,620 --> 00:11:07,420
You are such a dummy, I swear!

208
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:08,820
Go on!

209
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,240
If you've got something to say, by all means, say it!

210
00:11:11,780 --> 00:11:12,760
Nah, I'm set.

211
00:11:13,180 --> 00:11:16,700
If you're just gonna have a dumb tantrum, though, then I'll leave, dummy.

212
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:17,420
That's rich!

213
00:11:17,540 --> 00:11:18,880
The dummy's calling me dumb?

214
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:20,780
Man, you piss me off so much!

215
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:22,520
But...

216
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:26,560
Got so worked up, she smacked right into the doorframe.

217
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:27,400
Hard.

218
00:11:28,100 --> 00:11:29,540
Ugh...

219
00:11:29,540 --> 00:11:31,580
Okay, but what sparked this fight?

220
00:11:32,140 --> 00:11:33,920
I forgot like I always do.

221
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:38,740
This time, though, I won't budge until Hori says she's sorry!

222
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:40,480
How manly.

223
00:11:41,020 --> 00:11:42,140
Yeah, good luck.

224
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:45,600
The sheer nerve of this guy!

225
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:47,140
It didn't face him!

226
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:48,500
Not one bit!

227
00:11:49,360 --> 00:11:50,980
Miyamura's such a dummy!

228
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:52,740
There, there.

229
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:53,740
Don't cry.

230
00:11:54,340 --> 00:11:55,160
It's fine.

231
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:58,920
There isn't even another woman involved, so why are you getting this upset about it?

232
00:11:59,820 --> 00:12:01,360
Guys are just as dangerous.

233
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:03,240
I forgot you hit your head.

234
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:04,320
Get well soon, okay?

235
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:06,400
Wake up and tune in!

236
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:10,580
Just dump the guy.

237
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:11,360
No!

238
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:12,140
Why should I?

239
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:14,640
Look, I'll put it to you this way.

240
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:22,200
What do you do when you push him too far, and Miyamoto stops caring about you romantically or otherwise?

241
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:25,000
Nothing's guaranteed.

242
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:28,420
Even somebody you share a past with can always choose to leave.

243
00:12:28,420 --> 00:12:31,160
When Sengoku says it, I want to punch him.

244
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:33,740
But when Kono says it, I suddenly see the light.

245
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:35,000
Yeah.

246
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:36,200
Thanks, Kono.

247
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:37,160
Hey.

248
00:12:39,160 --> 00:12:41,100
I'm still angry as hell.

249
00:12:41,320 --> 00:12:42,580
This might take a minute.

250
00:12:44,340 --> 00:12:47,220
Time to submit our group's opinion, ladies and gentlemen.

251
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:50,580
You know what?

252
00:12:50,640 --> 00:12:52,040
I'll just make it my opinion.

253
00:12:52,740 --> 00:12:53,620
Go right ahead.

254
00:12:53,620 --> 00:12:58,360
Who cares if you answered at the same time?

255
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:00,520
Damn.

256
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:03,160
I'm more worn out than the combatants.

257
00:13:03,420 --> 00:13:05,020
I'm sorry you got involved, man.

258
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:07,700
Oh, but why am I angry?

259
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:08,540
Huh.

260
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,680
My brain's so exhausted I can't remember now.

261
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:14,980
If you're serious, this is going to go in an endless loop of spite.

262
00:13:15,680 --> 00:13:17,520
Just kiss and make up already.

263
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,460
I really would like to.

264
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:21,320
Oh.

265
00:13:21,740 --> 00:13:22,280
No touch.

266
00:13:22,280 --> 00:13:28,460
I see you've chosen death.

267
00:13:34,100 --> 00:13:35,420
Nabs and paper towels.

268
00:13:35,680 --> 00:13:36,640
Ew, you smell.

269
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:37,880
Look at that, I'll confuse you.

270
00:13:40,380 --> 00:13:41,760
What am I doing?

271
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:42,700
Jeez.

272
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:45,300
It's my fault.

273
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:47,520
So just say sorry and end it.

274
00:13:48,020 --> 00:13:49,120
Stop being stupid.

275
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:54,740
Hey, Miyamura.

276
00:13:55,640 --> 00:13:56,520
Have you seen Hori?

277
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:57,640
Why?

278
00:13:58,780 --> 00:14:00,820
She was absent from that last class.

279
00:14:01,360 --> 00:14:01,720
Huh?

280
00:14:02,100 --> 00:14:05,480
I went and checked the nurse's office and the girl's locker room.

281
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:06,860
But no dice.

282
00:14:07,100 --> 00:14:09,160
You went in the girl's locker room?

283
00:14:09,340 --> 00:14:11,340
Well, I'm getting kind of worried about her now.

284
00:14:11,340 --> 00:14:12,460
I'm worried you went in.

285
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:14,520
Wherever she went, she left her bag.

286
00:14:14,980 --> 00:14:16,300
Hope she's not out in that cold.

287
00:14:16,900 --> 00:14:17,340
Yeah.

288
00:14:18,420 --> 00:14:18,860
Wait.

289
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:19,840
Outside?

290
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:33,980
There she is.

291
00:14:36,980 --> 00:14:37,160
What?

292
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:38,080
Hmm?

293
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:43,540
Oh, um, nothing.

294
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:47,520
So it's over, right?

295
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:49,460
You stopped caring about me.

296
00:14:49,900 --> 00:14:50,240
Huh?

297
00:14:50,740 --> 00:14:53,660
Just because we have a past doesn't mean we have a future.

298
00:14:54,260 --> 00:14:54,440
Uh.

299
00:14:54,440 --> 00:14:58,160
I imagine you already hate me.

300
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:00,120
Why, Hori?

301
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:02,280
Why?

302
00:15:02,980 --> 00:15:04,280
Well, because...

303
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:07,240
Uh, you're crying?

304
00:15:07,580 --> 00:15:07,960
Seriously?

305
00:15:09,800 --> 00:15:10,780
Come on, now.

306
00:15:11,260 --> 00:15:12,540
There's nothing to cry about.

307
00:15:12,540 --> 00:15:14,540
But I...

308
00:15:14,540 --> 00:15:16,540
But I...

309
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:18,460
I constantly get irritated.

310
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,800
And then I take it out on you.

311
00:15:21,280 --> 00:15:22,600
It's so unfair.

312
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:25,600
Who knew she knew?

313
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:27,680
I want to look at you.

314
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:29,000
Just move your hands.

315
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:30,700
Please.

316
00:15:31,820 --> 00:15:32,300
There.

317
00:15:35,580 --> 00:15:37,720
Aw, you're really crying a river.

318
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:42,260
Prove that even monsters need a good cry.

319
00:15:42,680 --> 00:15:45,020
Your ears and nose turned crimson red, too.

320
00:15:46,560 --> 00:15:49,360
Falling like a baby in the middle of school?

321
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,280
That's tragic.

322
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:55,100
Shut your face!

323
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:56,360
How...

324
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:58,420
How are you always so freaking nice?

325
00:15:58,780 --> 00:16:02,720
Makes me think about dumb stuff like what I do if you started hating me!

326
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:06,300
Is that really what got you this worked up?

327
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:07,060
Jeez, Hori.

328
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:08,500
I swear.

329
00:16:08,780 --> 00:16:10,640
Though you named me the reigning dummy king,

330
00:16:10,940 --> 00:16:12,740
the crown suits you just as well.

331
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:15,360
I know I'm the queen to your king, okay?

332
00:16:15,620 --> 00:16:17,200
But you're still dumb or by a mile!

333
00:16:17,680 --> 00:16:19,320
You're surprisingly self-aware.

334
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:23,360
Granted, there is one thing you haven't realized.

335
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:26,620
And that's how very hard I've fallen for you.

336
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:29,600
Hating you would be difficult.

337
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:32,960
Dummy Morda strikes again!

338
00:16:33,060 --> 00:16:34,840
With the words in the eyes!

339
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:37,320
But I was being honest.

340
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:39,380
My bad.

341
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:41,740
Sorry, I like you.

342
00:16:45,060 --> 00:16:45,700
Dammit.

343
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:48,480
That wasn't at fault, but I apologized anyway.

344
00:16:48,480 --> 00:16:48,680
I'm sorry.

345
00:16:50,100 --> 00:16:50,580
Yeah!

346
00:16:50,820 --> 00:16:51,120
Duh!

347
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:53,360
You didn't do anything wrong, got that?

348
00:16:54,100 --> 00:16:56,720
I'm at fault a hundred out of a hundred times, all right?

349
00:16:57,140 --> 00:16:57,920
All right.

350
00:16:59,320 --> 00:17:01,260
Context would death help if I had it,

351
00:17:01,500 --> 00:17:02,160
but from up here,

352
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:04,460
that sure looked like a direct kick to the gut to me.

353
00:17:04,820 --> 00:17:05,460
It did.

354
00:17:07,060 --> 00:17:07,660
Scary.

355
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:11,120
Good morning.

356
00:17:12,080 --> 00:17:12,520
Hey.

357
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:14,820
Morning, Miyamura.

358
00:17:14,820 --> 00:17:18,580
A hoodie?

359
00:17:19,580 --> 00:17:21,080
So, that look is a choice.

360
00:17:21,320 --> 00:17:23,500
You shouldn't have been the one making it, though, for real.

361
00:17:23,940 --> 00:17:25,260
That's not quite your style.

362
00:17:25,560 --> 00:17:26,860
It looks warm, though.

363
00:17:27,240 --> 00:17:28,160
Gee, thanks.

364
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:30,400
Wow, this is a first.

365
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:32,160
Guess so.

366
00:17:32,540 --> 00:17:34,760
I wore this since my normal clothes were in the wash.

367
00:17:35,120 --> 00:17:35,480
Ah.

368
00:17:36,820 --> 00:17:38,600
Sometimes it's nice to spice it up.

369
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:42,300
You really think?

370
00:17:42,580 --> 00:17:42,840
Mm-hmm.

371
00:17:42,840 --> 00:17:44,920
Hey, friendos!

372
00:17:45,060 --> 00:17:47,060
Someone lend me their Japanese book!

373
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:48,580
Oh, whoa, Miyamura!

374
00:17:48,820 --> 00:17:49,500
Is that a hoodie?

375
00:17:49,780 --> 00:17:51,060
Trying to jack my style?

376
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:52,440
Negatory.

377
00:17:52,680 --> 00:17:54,080
She's not, but gay matching!

378
00:17:54,960 --> 00:17:57,440
I struggle to get this look to catch on each year

379
00:17:57,440 --> 00:17:58,780
when the cold has had its worst,

380
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:00,240
but it never, ever does!

381
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:03,260
Well, it is against the dress code.

382
00:18:04,100 --> 00:18:06,140
You're looking a little too sharp, though, Miyamura,

383
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:08,260
so why not add some flair to show it off, yeah?

384
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:09,500
Uh, okay.

385
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:11,620
He's violating the dress code,

386
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:13,300
and you want him to flaunt it?

387
00:18:14,100 --> 00:18:15,500
Oh, that's lit!

388
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:18,340
Put those shades back in the student council room, show!

389
00:18:18,700 --> 00:18:20,920
Put your fingers more like this.

390
00:18:21,300 --> 00:18:22,660
Dope, d-dope.

391
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:23,340
Enough!

392
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:25,720
Take your modern Japanese textbook

393
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:27,320
and go bother your own class!

394
00:18:27,320 --> 00:18:30,540
Now I'm gonna wonder why Shu's so big on hoodies

395
00:18:30,540 --> 00:18:31,540
for the rest of the day.

396
00:18:31,900 --> 00:18:34,420
Maybe they're like the ultimate item that he can equip.

397
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:37,420
Whereas my stats probably take a hit

398
00:18:37,420 --> 00:18:38,280
while I'm wearing a hoodie.

399
00:18:38,620 --> 00:18:40,340
Seems I gotta channel Iyuda, I guess,

400
00:18:40,460 --> 00:18:41,480
to rock this look.

401
00:18:42,860 --> 00:18:43,300
No.

402
00:18:44,300 --> 00:18:46,480
Do not make Iyuda your finish line.

403
00:18:46,940 --> 00:18:49,060
Strive to be like anybody except him.

404
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:50,020
Poor Iyuda.

405
00:18:50,020 --> 00:18:51,820
Ha!

406
00:18:52,100 --> 00:18:52,880
So it's true!

407
00:18:53,080 --> 00:18:54,400
You are breaking dress code!

408
00:18:54,560 --> 00:18:55,780
Morning, Mr. President.

409
00:18:56,140 --> 00:18:56,740
Good morning!

410
00:18:57,740 --> 00:18:59,740
I ran into Iyuda in the hall just now.

411
00:19:00,240 --> 00:19:02,640
He was thrilled to tell me you've adopted his style.

412
00:19:03,020 --> 00:19:05,040
More like I'm borrowing it for the day.

413
00:19:05,740 --> 00:19:07,800
Did you tell off Iyuda for his hoodie?

414
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:09,100
Don't play faves.

415
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:10,680
He's a lost cause.

416
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:12,380
I don't waste my breath on him,

417
00:19:12,640 --> 00:19:13,220
so no.

418
00:19:14,300 --> 00:19:15,240
Poor Iyuda.

419
00:19:15,240 --> 00:19:17,640
Yes, lunchtime!

420
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:21,600
Hey, the school got a new flavor of hot tea today.

421
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:22,500
You see it?

422
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:23,480
Not yet.

423
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:24,160
What is it?

424
00:19:24,460 --> 00:19:25,740
One you'll like, I'm sure.

425
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:27,220
To the tea!

426
00:19:28,240 --> 00:19:29,280
Hold up, Miyamura.

427
00:19:29,900 --> 00:19:30,140
Hmm?

428
00:19:30,740 --> 00:19:31,560
Your hut's rumbled.

429
00:19:32,100 --> 00:19:33,140
Oh, is it?

430
00:19:33,980 --> 00:19:34,800
Thank you.

431
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:36,720
If you're gonna break school rules,

432
00:19:36,820 --> 00:19:37,760
make it look good.

433
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:40,120
Huh?

434
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:41,880
Ah!

435
00:19:42,360 --> 00:19:42,840
Jeez!

436
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:44,340
What prompted you to do that?

437
00:19:44,340 --> 00:19:45,220
Curiosity?

438
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:46,140
Because that could be...

439
00:19:46,140 --> 00:19:46,660
Let's hurry!

440
00:19:48,880 --> 00:19:50,300
I can't fool Hori.

441
00:19:53,320 --> 00:19:54,180
What you think?

442
00:19:54,460 --> 00:19:55,220
Gonna wear it again?

443
00:19:55,680 --> 00:19:57,660
Nah, tomorrow it's back to my cardigan.

444
00:19:58,540 --> 00:19:59,180
Stare.

445
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:02,520
Stare.

446
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:07,380
Stare.

447
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:09,880
Miyamura!

448
00:20:10,220 --> 00:20:11,160
You coming over?

449
00:20:11,620 --> 00:20:12,000
Nope!

450
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,380
I need a head home today.

451
00:20:13,380 --> 00:20:14,380
See you later!

452
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:17,380
Do not tell me they had another fight.

453
00:20:17,840 --> 00:20:18,360
Okay.

454
00:20:22,360 --> 00:20:24,140
Hey, good morning, Hori.

455
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:25,520
Great morning.

456
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:27,040
This warm weather rocks.

457
00:20:27,260 --> 00:20:27,720
Yeah.

458
00:20:28,220 --> 00:20:29,160
Very sunny.

459
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:31,640
You're warm enough to ditch your scarf.

460
00:20:33,100 --> 00:20:33,740
Stare.

461
00:20:33,860 --> 00:20:34,020
Hmm?

462
00:20:35,280 --> 00:20:36,160
What's wrong?

463
00:20:36,160 --> 00:20:37,160
Come here a sec.

464
00:20:37,160 --> 00:20:39,860
Come here a sec.

465
00:20:43,120 --> 00:20:45,340
I'm getting kind of anxious about this.

466
00:20:48,460 --> 00:20:52,120
What are you...

467
00:20:52,120 --> 00:20:53,320
Yay!

468
00:20:55,820 --> 00:20:57,320
You smell like yourself again!

469
00:20:57,320 --> 00:20:57,880
Huh?

470
00:20:58,120 --> 00:20:58,980
That's, uh...

471
00:20:58,980 --> 00:20:59,320
Awesome!

472
00:21:00,660 --> 00:21:02,580
I should have known that's what she was up to.

473
00:21:02,960 --> 00:21:05,620
Miyamura, you have a wonderfully unique smell.

474
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,580
I was surprised when I couldn't pick it up from that white hoodie.

475
00:21:10,660 --> 00:21:11,300
Stare...

476
00:21:11,300 --> 00:21:12,300
Um...

477
00:21:12,300 --> 00:21:12,800
Um...

478
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:14,100
Cause it's Shindo's.

479
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:17,180
He left it at my apartment the last time he stayed over.

480
00:21:17,480 --> 00:21:18,300
I knew it.

481
00:21:19,260 --> 00:21:21,840
I ran it through the wash, so how did your nose know?

482
00:21:22,160 --> 00:21:23,720
Because it was obvious to me.

483
00:21:24,820 --> 00:21:26,800
Well, that makes one of us.

484
00:21:27,460 --> 00:21:31,480
I mean, your scent is my favorite smell in the entire world, Miyamura.

485
00:21:31,480 --> 00:21:36,480
Make sure that you return Shindo's hoodie, okay?

486
00:21:37,140 --> 00:21:37,240
Huh?

487
00:21:37,820 --> 00:21:38,320
Uh...

488
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:39,620
You're cold!

489
00:21:46,900 --> 00:21:47,520
Let's go.

490
00:21:48,280 --> 00:21:48,860
Uh...

491
00:21:48,860 --> 00:21:49,480
Yeah, let's...

492
00:21:50,800 --> 00:21:52,180
Just gonna leave it at that?

493
00:21:55,780 --> 00:21:56,100
Oh!

494
00:21:57,920 --> 00:21:58,640
Good morning!

495
00:21:59,760 --> 00:22:00,520
Good morning!

496
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:01,580
Uh-oh!

497
00:22:02,020 --> 00:22:02,680
What's up?

498
00:22:03,040 --> 00:22:04,320
Nothing but the sky.

499
00:22:04,980 --> 00:22:06,280
And it's a beautiful day.

500
00:22:19,660 --> 00:22:24,160
Then, I bought this much more, too.

501
00:22:24,640 --> 00:22:27,380
I bought a lot of things that I bought for you.

502
00:22:27,380 --> 00:22:29,800
I also got a lot of things that I bought for you.

503
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:30,800
I bought a lot of things that I bought for you.

504
00:22:30,800 --> 00:22:32,300
I bought a lot of things that I bought for you.

505
00:22:32,300 --> 00:23:02,280
Thank you.

506
00:23:02,300 --> 00:23:32,280
Thank you.

507
00:23:32,300 --> 00:23:34,300
Thank you.

